  formalisation: Price is not announced by anyone; it is what a settlement's own
    stock implies. Scarcity raises it, surplus lowers it, and the gap between two
    settlements' prices is what pays for a trade route.
  capability: 'Read a price the way this world sets one: rising as a good runs short,
    falling as it piles up.'
